{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2"],"primary":"c2","title":"Forbidding the Algorithmic Inflation of Rent (FAIR) Act","requirement":"Rental property owners (and their agents) may not pay or exchange consideration for the services of a coordinator, and coordinators may not facilitate agreements among owners that restrict competition, including by using algorithms that process competitors' competitively sensitive information to set or recommend rents, lease terms or occupancy levels. Parallel pricing coordination is also prohibited; violations are violations of the New Jersey Antitrust Act, and the Attorney General must establish a complaint location and may adopt rules.","key_value":"Ban on using algorithmic coordinators and on parallel pricing coordination for residential rentals","status":"not_yet_effective","effective_date":"2027-07-01","end_date":null,"citation":"P.L.2026, c.43","coverage_conditions":"Applies to all residential dwelling units in the State (houses, apartments, accessory units or other units intended as a primary residence), and to rental property owners, their agents, representatives or subcontractors, and coordinators.","exemptions":"Residential dwelling unit excludes inpatient medical care, licensed long-term care, and detention or correctional facilities. Government entities setting or limiting rents through affordability controls are not coordinators. The following are not algorithmic devices or are excluded: spreadsheets operating without AI and requiring human analysis, databases that only use an algorithm to query unprocessed data, research or testing not used for pricing, free public rent estimates, and equal-terms real estate brokerage databases that do not set or recommend prices.","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
